[h1]Phobos Shipbreaker[/h1]
[h2]Pending-construction room-load mitigation in 0.19.1[/h2]
Requires Phobos Framework 0.21.1 or newer. When pending Shipbreaker equipment reduces the initial loading grid, restore checked saved bounds before native room/zone assignments. Retain saved atmosphere and construction progress. This cannot recover gas already lost before saving. The owner reported a successful affected-save reload on 26 September 2026; broader save/reload coverage remains unverified.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-room-load-mitigation.md]Evidence, limits and reload check[/url]
[h2]Shared completion cues in 0.19.0[/h2]
Requires Phobos Framework 0.22.0 or newer. D4/R4 watches now use the shared Phobos volume/mute and one audio channel across mods. Existing one-batch meaning and original sound remain; no new furnace, transfer or ambient cues. Gameplay/listening review pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shared-completion-cues.md]Shared controls and limits[/url]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.20.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Recover useful shipbuilding materials and manage onboard industry with Phobos' Rivetline equipment and the Phobos' Asterel C1 Industrial Control Console.

[h2]Current features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Process manually supplied detached wall panels; connect a grabber, wall chute and indoor dismantling fixture.
[*]Recover steel and aluminium from identified processing residue, retaining finite rejects.
[*]Pair collectors and material routes explicitly; manage machines through local Control Panels, C1 or F3.
[*]Optionally watch one D4/R4 batch: a brief quiet tone and visible status confirm products committed to its output tray. Volume/mute follows native sound-effects volume; further queued batches stay silent.
[*]Cast aluminium housings with the electrically heated F6 furnace and finite cooling.
[*]Choose existing direct exterior or underside cooling, or optional F6-C sealed conduits to a remote F6-R radiator.
[*]INSTALL catalogue: APPS for D4, grabber, chute, collector, R4 and F6; HVAC for F6-R, F6-P and F6-C; CTRL for C1. Intact and damaged forms retain normal physical installation requirements. Prepared; gameplay review pending.
[/list]

[h2]Limits and save behaviour[/h2]
[list]
[*]Experimental candidate; current machinery and artwork still need in-game evaluation.
[*]No attached-hull cutting, persistent cargo ejection or perfect recycling. Recipe yields are authored gameplay budgets.
[*]Processing and receiving are separate permissions and pause after reload. Saved links are retained.
[*]Completion watches are session-only and clear on processing Pause/Cancel, fault or reload. Audio is restricted to the requesting selected crew on the same ship. Muted or suppressed events are never replayed. Listening evaluation is pending; no guaranteed native alarm suppression.
[*]Cooling uses a simplified thermal model with optional finite coolant servicing. Direct coupling can transfer furnace heat without power; piped circulation requires electricity. On power loss, the radiator still rejects its own stored heat and the furnace retains bounded room leakage. Piped circulation adds up to 1 kW; cold feed motors use 2 kW by default. Existing direct and legacy sealed installations retain their saved meaning.
[/list]

[h2]Original trial in 0.18.0[/h2]
First optional watched-batch audio trial: one original 280 ms tone after a D4/R4 output commit, with quiet volume/mute, explicit watch/unwatch controls and no queued playback. No new furnace, navigation or ambient cues; existing material routes and saves retain their meaning. Reclaimer fallback controls now scroll.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-completion-cue.md]Completion cue controls and listening checks[/url]

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
The following requirements describe the current prepared candidate. Future autonomous-reclamation work will require Auto Nav with an existing N1 or N2 module, as selected by the owner. That dependency change and the automation are not implemented yet.

Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.22.0 or newer. Auto Nav and Agriculture are optional. No Crafting Framework or Salvage Workshop dependency.

This is a maintained pre-publication page draft, not a download announcement. No Workshop item has been published for this draft. Use the installation guide for source/prepared-package availability and loader setup. Do not remove required providers from saves that contain their content.

