[h2]Support and credits[/h2]
[b]Research only, held from feature claims:[/b] autonomous reclamation is specified around one player-selected G4 after manual valuables recovery. The first proposed slice aligns and holds the G4, cuts/feeds one wall and advances along a short section. Docking/capture is optional. Collision-compatible reach and checked processing during gentle positioning remain unresolved; broader recipes, storage, repeated furnace operation and whole-wreck completion remain future work. No automatic cutting, invisible long reach or cargo disposal is supplied by this draft.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-autopilot-research.md]Autonomous reclamation research[/url] | [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-autopilot-handover.md]Implementation sequence[/url]
[url=https://www.nasa.gov/general/nasas-hybrid-computer-enables-ravens-autonomous-rendezvous-capability/]NASA Goddard's Raven research[/url] and [url=https://www.esa.int/Science_Exploration/Human_and_Robotic_Exploration/ATV/ATV_views_Space_Station_as_never_before]ESA's LIRIS experiment, developed by Airbus with Jena Optronik and Sodern[/url] inform the sensing proposal. Blue Bottle Games' inspected native engine determines game boundaries; finite reach, work rates and yields are authored gameplay choices. No institutional or author endorsement or mod validation is implied.

